  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 10 tests for it in `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes with all 12 tests, including the two existing `capitalize` ones.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Diacritics:** `đ`/`Đ` becomes `d`, then the text is split into base letters plus combining accent marks and the marks are removed.\n- **Cleanup:** the text is lowercased and every run of characters outside a-z or 0-9 becomes a single hyphen. Leading hyphens are trimmed.\n- **Length:** the result is cut to 50 characters, then trailing hyphens are trimmed, so a slug cut at 50 can't end with a hyphen.\n\n**Tests cover:**\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics.\n- `đ`/`Đ`.\n- Collapsing runs of punctuation and spaces.\n- Trimming hyphens at both ends.\n- Digits.\n- Empty and symbol-only input.\n- Truncation at 50, including a hyphen landing on the 50th character.\n\nNon-string input is converted with `String(text)`, so `null` gives `'null'`. Your spec didn't cover that case, so say if you want it to return an empty string instead.",
